-- FX / Animation Logger (client-side LocalScript) - Dex-style windows
--
-- v7: Design Screen buttons now have an "Anim type": AnimationId / Frames / Frames+VFX / Frames+SFX /
--     Full-FX / Full-FX+cutscene / Full-FX everything. Pick one and the script is generated and stored
--     inside the button automatically (it works without the original animation).
--     "Save all" (anim entries, line 3) keeps keyframes + effects + code: Saved tab > Saved edits.
-- v14: Cutscene camera: caught more reliably (Custom camera moved by the game, short gaps, no root, long cutscenes, a cutscene with
--      many effects no longer drops its camera). Saving an edited animation again no longer REPLACES the earlier save: the older one
--      stays in Saved edits as "(older save ...)". Search tab: every VFX / SFX instance is listed (full settings, no merging by name),
--      plus sound ids kept in values and everything the logger saw this session.
-- v14b: 2D logging (full-screen GUI cutscenes, images, titles, flashes: recorded with their animation and replayed), "Find related"
--       button in the FX editor (models / FX / sounds / 2D things that match the animation), moving one FX no longer shifts the others.
-- v13: FX LIBRARY: save any effect (FX editor panel / "All to lib", VFX / SFX / OBJ tabs, Search tab) and add it to ANY other animation
--      (FX editor > Lib, or Saved tab > FX Library). Reset all (Anim Editor) / Reset (FX editor) now go back to the GAME's original, and a saved copy is
--      never touched by a reset (Saved tab, Design Screen and "Saved edits" copy the SAVED version, not the live working copy). New "Saved" buttons bring the saved
--      copy back. Search: more effect classes, no 4000 cap, same-name effects with different settings are listed separately, rows are no longer dropped.
--      VFX / SFX tabs also log effects that appear next to you during one of YOUR animations even with "Own character only" on. FX editor search also reads ids / classes.
-- v12: Search tab finds VFX + SFX too (Anim / VFX / SFX chips). A saved EDIT is now what every saved copy uses
--      (before, the kept ORIGINAL frames won after a rejoin). Effects: "Log EVERYTHING during a move" setting (default ON),
--      PlayLocalSound / PlayOnRemove sounds caught, rigs outside a Model supported. Cutscene camera: recorded for the whole
--      cutscene animation and attached (trimmed to the animation) to every animation it overlaps.
-- v11: Rename (FX editor, Anim editor, Saved tab). New OBJ tab (spawned objects + cutscene cameras).
--      Cutscenes: camera counts as taken over for Fixed/Watch/Attach/Track/Scriptable, a camera pointed at something
--      that is not you, or far away; animations that started just BEFORE the takeover are logged afterwards.
--      FX editor: Bulk (turn off / on / delete many by name, time, type) and + FX/OBJ (add sound, particles, light, objects).
--      Finished script: move buttons use the same ContextActionService method as the JJS moveset (real input + title,
--      size / position re-applied every 0.5s from the button's parent).
-- v10: the finished script draws NOTHING of its own: move buttons are ContextActionService touch buttons,
--      the joystick is Roblox's own thumbstick (loco anims follow how far you push it) and the jump uses
--      Roblox's own jump button. The jump button's Anim type covers BOTH the jump and the fall animation.
-- v9: fixed the finished script drawing every button / joystick / jump button at 0x0 (invisible).
-- v8: the jump button and the joystick have an Anim type too (jump anim / idle, walk, run, ... anims).
--     In the finished script the move + jump buttons are real ContextActionService touch buttons (like the
--     game's own mobile buttons) and the whole screen is parented where games cannot wipe it.
--
-- Run it again any time: the old logger window is closed and replaced by the new one.
-- New: Block for VFX / SFX | red scrub line + Pause in Preview, FX Editor and Anim Editor (the dummy and the effects follow it)
--      3D Viewer (spin / zoom) | Save edits (Saved tab > Saved edits, view + edit their code) | floating Design Screen
--      Settings > "Log move variants" (off) and "Only this move's own effects" (on).
-- Tabs: Animations | VFX | SFX | Search (every animation in the game) | Filters | Settings | Console
-- Search tab: Scan game -> type to filter -> Copy / Full+FX / Preview / VIEW FULL CODE / Capture.
-- Live preview: plays an animation (+ its recorded FX) on a clone of your character in front of you.
-- Player filter / Compact mode / window size presets / extra FX capture options: Settings tab.
-- Defaults: "Own character only" and "Unique only" are ON (turn them off in Settings).
-- Themes: Settings > Appearance (Dex Dark, Old Logger, Midnight Blue, Dracula, Forest, Crimson,
--         Ocean, AMOLED Black, Sunset, Solarized Dark). The choice is saved.
--
-- Top-bar tabs:  Animations | VFX | SFX | Filters | Settings | Console
-- Settings (excluded / blocked lists, options, quality, window position) are saved to
-- "AnimVFXLogger_Settings.json" in your executor's workspace folder and restored next time.
--
-- ANIM entry:  line 1 = the important buttons:  Copy | Full+FX | Run | VIEW FULL CODE
--              Copy = frame-by-frame script (no original animation needed)
--              Full+FX = that script + the VFX/SFX that played with the animation
--              line 2 = Code (plain "play this AnimationId" script) | ID | Stop | Block | Excl | RBXMX
-- VFX entry:   Copy = script that rebuilds the effect from its properties (no asset needed)
-- SFX entry:   Copy = script that just plays the sound
-- Every VFX/SFX in a script runs inside pcall - if one fails, the animation still plays.
--
-- Frame-by-frame generation is fast: it reads the animation's real keyframes when the game
-- lets us (instant), otherwise it captures on a hidden rig at up to 4x speed.
-- "Quality" (Settings tab / viewer) drops frames that can be rebuilt by blending the neighbours.

